import QtslAux.QuantumSheaf
import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Category.Cat

/-! # Categorified descent on the derived diamond site: the attained-regime equivalence and the multiplicity obstruction

`QtslAux.QuantumSheaf` closed the 1-truncated story: the state presheaf
of an overlap-attained net is a sheaf at derived covers, and the
morphism-level (endomorphism) shadow of descent holds under
multiplicative generation.  This module climbs one categorical level:
representation *categories* in place of state *sets*, descent *data*
with gluing isomorphisms and a cocycle condition in place of compatible
families, and the comparison *functor* in place of the amalgamation
map.  It is the categorified core of the stack condition of
Benini–Grant-Stuart–Schenkel (arXiv:2404.14510, §2.2) for a
Haag–Kastler-style net (Haag–Kastler, J. Math. Phys. 5, 848 (1964)) on
the derived diamond site, at finite-dimensional matrix grade, in four
movements.

* **The attained-regime equivalence, at the canonical cover.**
  `descentComparison` sends a representation of the global algebra to
  its restriction datum.  At the sieve generated by the chronological
  interior (`interiorSieve` — the canonical covering sieve of the
  derived topology) it is an equivalence of categories
  (`descentComparison_isEquivalence_interior`) whenever the global
  algebra is attained on an interior witness and the interior family is
  directed.  Directedness is not an extra axiom: the filtered/directed
  fields of a `ChronologyKit` — precisely the fields the derived
  coverage never consumes (`diamondTopology_factors`) — *are* interior
  directedness (`ChronologyKit.interior_directed`).  This is the first
  place in the development where the descent half of bicontinuity is
  consumed, and it is consumed by the categorical layer that states
  could not see: transporting *multiplicity* (dimension) data between
  fibres.  The two-qubit instance is `qubitNet_stack_attained`.

* **The multiplicity obstruction at the spacelike pair-cover.**
  Essential surjectivity fails at the pair cover: `wingDatum` assigns
  to each wing its two-dimensional irreducible representation
  (multiplicity one) — a lawful descent datum, scalar-tied at the
  overlap — and no global representation restricts to it
  (`wingDatum_not_in_essImage`).  Any gluing candidate is forced to
  dimension two by a trace argument, and the global algebra has no
  unital two-dimensional representation
  (`no_unital_hom_top_to_dim_two`): the four diagonal matrix units
  would map to idempotents with equal traces summing to two, and a
  `2 × 2` idempotent of trace `½` is refuted by entry arithmetic.
  Quantum composition is tensorial — global dimension is the *product*
  of wing dimensions, not their common value — and that arithmetic is
  exactly what cover-type object gluing cannot express.

* **Fullness is about connectivity, not generation.**  The landed
  halves `D₁`, `D₂` touch at a single point — the null corner `(0,0)`
  of the interval between the sites — and that corner, as a member of
  the pair sieve, ties the two wings' components together in any
  descent morphism.  Hence the comparison at the landed pair cover is
  *fully faithful* (`descentComparison_pair_full`): the corner tie
  makes the wing components agree, and multiplicative generation
  (`adjoin_union_eq_top`, through the two-sided intertwiner extension
  `intertwines_of_le_adjoin`) extends the common matrix to a global
  intertwiner.  Multiplicative generation *alone* does not suffice: for
  a gapped right half (`gappedD₂` — same wing algebra, same generation,
  empty overlap with `D₁`) fullness fails
  (`descentComparison_gapped_not_full`): the wings carry independent
  endomorphism freedoms that only a connected cover synchronizes.  So
  the ES/FF split of the stack condition is displayed at one cover: at
  the kissing pair cover the morphism clause holds whole and the object
  clause fails on multiplicity.

* **The fences.**  The equivalence is a statement about the canonical
  cover, not about every covering sieve: the derived topology certifies
  the *empty* sieve at a degenerate (corner) diamond — no subdiamond of
  a point is chronologically interior — and over the empty sieve the
  comparison is not even faithful
  (`descentComparison_corner_not_faithful`), because representation
  categories, unlike state sets, are not points over scalar fibres.
  And the bad object of arXiv:2404.14510, Proposition 3.3 fails
  *fullness* at the canonical cover (`badNet_not_full_interior`):
  content concentrated at the global scale is invisible to the interior
  at morphism grade too, so the attainment hypothesis of the
  equivalence is load-bearing exactly where the separation-grade story
  already needed it.

Throughout, representations are unital algebra homomorphisms into
`Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ` (`FinRep`), morphisms are intertwiners, and
descent data over a sieve on the thin diamond site carry their cocycle
condition at matrix level.  Direct integrals and W*-completeness
(Henriques–Nivedita–Penneys, arXiv:2411.01678) appear nowhere: the
attained regime needs none of them, which is the finite-dimensional
form of the claim that completeness enters only the directed-regime
object clause.  Interiority as order-grade relative compactness is
Martin–Panangaden, arXiv:gr-qc/0407094; the cosheaf-side failure for
algebras is arXiv:1903.02878, Appendix A.
-/

namespace Qtsl
namespace QuantumStack

open CategoryTheory Matrix DiamondSite QuantumDescent QuantumStates QuantumSheaf
open scoped Kronecker

/-! ## Finite-dimensional representations and intertwiners -/

/-- A finite-dimensional representation of a ℂ-algebra: a unital algebra
homomorphism into a matrix algebra.  The dimension is data, so the
multiplicity bookkeeping of descent is type-visible. -/
structure FinRep (A : Type*) [Ring A] [Algebra ℂ A] where
  /-- the dimension of the representation space -/
  dim : ℕ
  /-- the action -/
  π : A →ₐ[ℂ] Matrix (Fin dim) (Fin dim) ℂ

namespace FinRep

variable {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra ℂ A]

/-- Morphisms of representations: intertwining matrices. -/
@[ext]
structure Hom (ρ σ : FinRep A) where
  /-- the underlying matrix, mapping the source space to the target -/
  val : Matrix (Fin σ.dim) (Fin ρ.dim) ℂ
  intertwine : ∀ a : A, σ.π a * val = val * ρ.π a

@[reducible] noncomputable instance : Category (FinRep A) where
  Hom := Hom
  id ρ := ⟨1, fun a => by rw [mul_one, one_mul]⟩
  comp {ρ σ τ} f g := ⟨g.val * f.val, fun a => by
    rw [← Matrix.mul_assoc, g.intertwine a, Matrix.mul_assoc, f.intertwine a,
      ← Matrix.mul_assoc]⟩
  id_comp f := Hom.ext (Matrix.mul_one _)
  comp_id f := Hom.ext (Matrix.one_mul _)
  assoc f g h := Hom.ext (Matrix.mul_assoc _ _ _).symm

@[simp] theorem id_val (ρ : FinRep A) : (𝟙 ρ : ρ ⟶ ρ).val = 1 := rfl

@[simp] theorem comp_val {ρ σ τ : FinRep A} (f : ρ ⟶ σ) (g : σ ⟶ τ) :
    (f ≫ g).val = g.val * f.val := rfl

/-- Pulling a representation back along an algebra homomorphism:
precomposition.  Functorial on the nose. -/
@[reducible] noncomputable def pull {B : Type*} [Ring B] [Algebra ℂ B] (f : B →ₐ[ℂ] A) :
    FinRep A ⥤ FinRep B where
  obj ρ := ⟨ρ.dim, ρ.π.comp f⟩
  map T := ⟨T.val, fun b => T.intertwine (f b)⟩
  map_id _ := rfl
  map_comp _ _ := rfl

@[simp] theorem pull_obj_dim {B : Type*} [Ring B] [Algebra ℂ B]
    (f : B →ₐ[ℂ] A) (ρ : FinRep A) : ((pull f).obj ρ).dim = ρ.dim := rfl

@[simp] theorem pull_obj_π {B : Type*} [Ring B] [Algebra ℂ B]
    (f : B →ₐ[ℂ] A) (ρ : FinRep A) (b : B) :
    ((pull f).obj ρ).π b = ρ.π (f b) := rfl

@[simp] theorem pull_map_val {B : Type*} [Ring B] [Algebra ℂ B]
    (f : B →ₐ[ℂ] A) {ρ σ : FinRep A} (T : ρ ⟶ σ) :
    ((pull f).map T).val = T.val := rfl

/-- Isomorphic representations have equal dimensions: the two
composition identities have traces `dim` and `dim'`, and trace is
cyclic. -/
theorem dim_eq_of_iso {ρ σ : FinRep A} (e : ρ ≅ σ) : ρ.dim = σ.dim := by
  have h1 : e.inv.val * e.hom.val = 1 := by
    have h := congrArg Hom.val e.hom_inv_id
    rw [comp_val, id_val] at h
    exact h
  have h2 : e.hom.val * e.inv.val = 1 := by
    have h := congrArg Hom.val e.inv_hom_id
    rw [comp_val, id_val] at h
    exact h
  have htr := congrArg Matrix.trace h1
  rw [Matrix.trace_mul_comm, h2, Matrix.trace_one, Matrix.trace_one] at htr
  simp only [Fintype.card_fin] at htr
  exact_mod_cast htr.symm

end FinRep

/-- The tautological four-dimensional representation of a subalgebra of
the two-qubit matrix algebra: include, then reindex `Fin 2 × Fin 2` to
`Fin 4`. -/
@[reducible] noncomputable def tautRep (A : Subalgebra ℂ TwoQubits) : FinRep ↥A :=
  ⟨4, ((Matrix.reindexAlgEquiv ℂ ℂ
    (finProdFinEquiv : Fin 2 × Fin 2 ≃ Fin 4)).toAlgHom).comp A.val⟩

@[simp] theorem tautRep_dim (A : Subalgebra ℂ TwoQubits) :
    (tautRep A).dim = 4 := rfl

theorem tautRep_π_apply (A : Subalgebra ℂ TwoQubits) (a : ↥A) :
    (tautRep A).π a = Matrix.reindexAlgEquiv ℂ ℂ
      (finProdFinEquiv : Fin 2 × Fin 2 ≃ Fin 4) a.val := rfl

/-- The representation prestack packaged as a functor to `Cat` — the
categorified object the descent comparison probes.  Functoriality is
definitional: pulls compose on the nose, because algebra homomorphisms
do. -/
noncomputable def repFunctor {X : Type*} [PartialOrder X]
    {n : Type*} [Fintype n] [DecidableEq n] (N : ObservableNet X n) :
    (Diamond X)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Cat where
  obj D := Cat.of (FinRep ↥(N.alg D.unop))
  map f :=
    (FinRep.pull (Subalgebra.inclusion (N.isotone (leOfHom f.unop)))).toCatHom
  map_id _ := Cat.Hom.ext rfl
  map_comp _ _ := Cat.Hom.ext rfl

/-! ## Descent data over a sieve on the diamond site

The diamond poset is thin, so descent data need no coherence beyond a
single cocycle condition, and that condition is stated at matrix level:
the gluing isomorphisms compose as matrices.  This is the strict form
appropriate to a site with proof-irrelevant morphisms — the bilimit
form of arXiv:2404.14510 collapses to it over a poset. -/

variable {X : Type*} [PartialOrder X]
variable {n : Type*} [Fintype n] [DecidableEq n]

/-- A descent datum for an observable net over a sieve: a representation
of the local algebra over each member, gluing isomorphisms along
refinements, and the matrix-level cocycle condition. -/
structure DescentDatum (N : ObservableNet X n) (D : Diamond X) (S : Sieve D) where
  /-- the component at a sieve member -/
  obj : ∀ ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (h : E ≤ D), S.arrows (homOfLE h) → FinRep ↥(N.alg E)
  /-- gluing: the component at a refinement is identified with the
  restricted component -/
  glue : ∀ ⦃E F : Diamond X⦄ (hEF : E ≤ F) (hFD : F ≤ D)
    (hSF : S.arrows (homOfLE hFD)) (hSE : S.arrows (homOfLE (hEF.trans hFD))),
    obj (hEF.trans hFD) hSE ≅
      (FinRep.pull (Subalgebra.inclusion (N.isotone hEF))).obj (obj hFD hSF)
  /-- the cocycle condition, at matrix level -/
  cocycle : ∀ ⦃E F G : Diamond X⦄ (hEF : E ≤ F) (hFG : F ≤ G) (hGD : G ≤ D)
    (hSG : S.arrows (homOfLE hGD)) (hSF : S.arrows (homOfLE (hFG.trans hGD)))
    (hSE : S.arrows (homOfLE ((hEF.trans hFG).trans hGD))),
    (glue hFG hGD hSG hSF).hom.val * (glue hEF (hFG.trans hGD) hSF hSE).hom.val
      = (glue (hEF.trans hFG) hGD hSG hSE).hom.val

namespace DescentDatum

variable {N : ObservableNet X n} {D : Diamond X} {S : Sieve D}

/-- Morphisms of descent data: componentwise intertwiners, compatible
with the gluing isomorphisms at matrix level. -/
@[ext]
structure Hom (Xd Yd : DescentDatum N D S) where
  /-- the componentwise intertwiners -/
  app : ∀ ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (h : E ≤ D) (hS : S.arrows (homOfLE h)),
    Xd.obj h hS ⟶ Yd.obj h hS
  compat : ∀ ⦃E F : Diamond X⦄ (hEF : E ≤ F) (hFD : F ≤ D)
    (hSF : S.arrows (homOfLE hFD)) (hSE : S.arrows (homOfLE (hEF.trans hFD))),
    (Yd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).hom.val * (app (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).val
      = (app hFD hSF).val * (Xd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).hom.val

theorem Hom.ext' {Xd Yd : DescentDatum N D S} {u v : Hom Xd Yd}
    (h : ∀ ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (hE : E ≤ D) (hS : S.arrows (homOfLE hE)),
      u.app hE hS = v.app hE hS) : u = v := by
  cases u; cases v
  congr 1
  funext E hE hS
  exact h hE hS

@[reducible] noncomputable instance : Category (DescentDatum N D S) where
  Hom := Hom
  id Xd := ⟨fun _ h hS => 𝟙 _, fun hEF hFD hSF hSE => by
    simp⟩
  comp {Xd Yd Zd} u v := ⟨fun _ h hS => u.app h hS ≫ v.app h hS,
    fun {E F} hEF hFD hSF hSE => by
      simp only [FinRep.comp_val]
      calc (Zd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).hom.val *
            ((v.app (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).val * (u.app (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).val)
          = ((Zd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).hom.val *
              (v.app (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).val) *
              (u.app (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).val := by
            rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]
        _ = ((v.app hFD hSF).val * (Yd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).hom.val) *
              (u.app (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).val := by rw [v.compat]
        _ = (v.app hFD hSF).val * ((Yd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).hom.val *
              (u.app (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).val) := by rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]
        _ = (v.app hFD hSF).val * ((u.app hFD hSF).val *
              (Xd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).hom.val) := by rw [u.compat]
        _ = ((v.app hFD hSF).val * (u.app hFD hSF).val) *
              (Xd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).hom.val := by rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]⟩
  id_comp u := Hom.ext' (fun _ hE hS => Category.id_comp _)
  comp_id u := Hom.ext' (fun _ hE hS => Category.comp_id _)
  assoc u v w := Hom.ext' (fun _ hE hS => Category.assoc _ _ _)

@[simp] theorem id_app {Xd : DescentDatum N D S} ⦃E : Diamond X⦄
    (h : E ≤ D) (hS : S.arrows (homOfLE h)) :
    (𝟙 Xd : Xd ⟶ Xd).app h hS = 𝟙 (Xd.obj h hS) := rfl

@[simp] theorem comp_app {Xd Yd Zd : DescentDatum N D S}
    (u : Xd ⟶ Yd) (v : Yd ⟶ Zd) ⦃E : Diamond X⦄
    (h : E ≤ D) (hS : S.arrows (homOfLE h)) :
    (u ≫ v).app h hS = u.app h hS ≫ v.app h hS := rfl

/-- Matrix-level inverse identity for a gluing isomorphism. -/
theorem glue_inv_hom (Xd : DescentDatum N D S) ⦃E F : Diamond X⦄
    (hEF : E ≤ F) (hFD : F ≤ D) (hSF : S.arrows (homOfLE hFD))
    (hSE : S.arrows (homOfLE (hEF.trans hFD))) :
    (Xd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).inv.val * (Xd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).hom.val
      = 1 := by
  have h := congrArg FinRep.Hom.val (Xd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).hom_inv_id
  rw [FinRep.comp_val, FinRep.id_val] at h
  exact h

/-- Matrix-level inverse identity for a gluing isomorphism. -/
theorem glue_hom_inv (Xd : DescentDatum N D S) ⦃E F : Diamond X⦄
    (hEF : E ≤ F) (hFD : F ≤ D) (hSF : S.arrows (homOfLE hFD))
    (hSE : S.arrows (homOfLE (hEF.trans hFD))) :
    (Xd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).hom.val * (Xd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).inv.val
      = 1 := by
  have h := congrArg FinRep.Hom.val (Xd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).inv_hom_id
  rw [FinRep.comp_val, FinRep.id_val] at h
  exact h

end DescentDatum

/-! ## The comparison functor -/

/-- The descent comparison: a representation of the global algebra
restricts to a descent datum with definitional gluing. -/
@[reducible] noncomputable def descentComparison (N : ObservableNet X n) (D : Diamond X)
    (S : Sieve D) : FinRep ↥(N.alg D) ⥤ DescentDatum N D S where
  obj ρ :=
    { obj := fun _ h _ =>
        (FinRep.pull (Subalgebra.inclusion (N.isotone h))).obj ρ
      glue := fun _ _ _ _ _ _ => Iso.refl _
      cocycle := fun _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => by simp }
  map {ρ σ} T :=
    { app := fun _ h _ =>
        (FinRep.pull (Subalgebra.inclusion (N.isotone h))).map T
      compat := fun _ _ _ _ => by simp }
  map_id ρ := DescentDatum.Hom.ext' (fun _ hE hS => rfl)
  map_comp T T' := DescentDatum.Hom.ext' (fun _ hE hS => rfl)

@[simp] theorem descentComparison_obj_obj (N : ObservableNet X n)
    (D : Diamond X) (S : Sieve D) (ρ : FinRep ↥(N.alg D))
    ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (h : E ≤ D) (hS : S.arrows (homOfLE h)) :
    ((descentComparison N D S).obj ρ).obj h hS =
      (FinRep.pull (Subalgebra.inclusion (N.isotone h))).obj ρ := rfl

@[simp] theorem descentComparison_obj_glue_hom_val (N : ObservableNet X n)
    (D : Diamond X) (S : Sieve D) (ρ : FinRep ↥(N.alg D))
    ⦃E F : Diamond X⦄ (hEF : E ≤ F) (hFD : F ≤ D)
    (hSF : S.arrows (homOfLE hFD))
    (hSE : S.arrows (homOfLE (hEF.trans hFD))) :
    (((descentComparison N D S).obj ρ).glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).hom.val = 1 :=
  rfl

@[simp] theorem descentComparison_map_app_val (N : ObservableNet X n)
    (D : Diamond X) (S : Sieve D) {ρ σ : FinRep ↥(N.alg D)} (T : ρ ⟶ σ)
    ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (h : E ≤ D) (hS : S.arrows (homOfLE h)) :
    (((descentComparison N D S).map T).app h hS).val = T.val := rfl

/-- Components of a morphism between comparison images share one
underlying matrix along any refinement inside the sieve. -/
theorem theta_app_val_eq {N : ObservableNet X n} {D : Diamond X}
    {S : Sieve D} {ρ σ : FinRep ↥(N.alg D)}
    (u : (descentComparison N D S).obj ρ ⟶ (descentComparison N D S).obj σ)
    {E F : Diamond X} (hE : E ≤ D) (hEF : E ≤ F) (hFD : F ≤ D)
    (hSF : S.arrows (homOfLE hFD)) (hSE : S.arrows (homOfLE hE)) :
    (u.app hE hSE).val = (u.app hFD hSF).val := by
  have h := u.compat hEF hFD hSF hSE
  simp only [Iso.refl_hom, FinRep.id_val, Matrix.one_mul,
    Matrix.mul_one] at h
  show (u.app (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).val = (u.app hFD hSF).val
  exact h

/-! ## Interior directedness: the descent half of a chronology kit -/

/-- Directedness of the chronologically interior family beneath a
diamond. -/
def InteriorDirected (M : MixingKit X) (D : Diamond X) : Prop :=
  ∀ ⦃E F : Diamond X⦄, M.interiorMem D E → M.interiorMem D F →
    ∃ H : Diamond X, M.interiorMem D H ∧ E ≤ H ∧ F ≤ H

/-- **The filtered/directed fields of a chronology kit are interior
directedness**: `up_filtered` at the lower tip and `down_directed` at
the upper tip produce a common interior upper bound — no interpolation,
no mixing.  These are exactly the fields the derived coverage never
consumes (`diamondTopology_factors`): the coverage half and the descent
half of bicontinuity part ways at the site and reunite here, one
categorical level up. -/
theorem _root_.Qtsl.DiamondSite.ChronologyKit.interior_directed
    (K : ChronologyKit X) (D : Diamond X) :
    InteriorDirected K.toMixingKit D := by
  intro E F hE hF
  obtain ⟨l, hDl, hlE, hlF⟩ := K.up_filtered hE.1 hF.1
  obtain ⟨h, hhD, hEh, hFh⟩ := K.down_directed hE.2 hF.2
  exact ⟨⟨l, h, hlE.trans (E.le.trans hEh)⟩, ⟨hDl, hhD⟩, ⟨hlE, hEh⟩,
    ⟨hlF, hFh⟩⟩

/-! ## Faithfulness -/

/-- The comparison is faithful at any inhabited sieve: a component's
underlying matrix is the morphism's matrix. -/
theorem descentComparison_faithful (N : ObservableNet X n) (D : Diamond X)
    (S : Sieve D) {E₁ : Diamond X} (h₁ : E₁ ≤ D)
    (hS₁ : S.arrows (homOfLE h₁)) :
    (descentComparison N D S).Faithful where
  map_injective {ρ σ} {T T'} h := by
    apply FinRep.Hom.ext
    have := congrArg (fun (u : (descentComparison N D S).obj ρ ⟶
      (descentComparison N D S).obj σ) => (u.app h₁ hS₁).val) h
    simpa using this

/-! ## Fullness at the canonical cover (attained regime) -/

/-- **Fullness at the canonical cover**: with an interior attainment
witness and a directed interior family, every morphism of restriction
data is the restriction of a global intertwiner.  The witness component
supplies the matrix; directedness ties every other component to it. -/
theorem descentComparison_full_interior (M : MixingKit X)
    (N : ObservableNet X n) {D E₀ : Diamond X} (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (halg : N.alg D ≤ N.alg E₀) (hdir : InteriorDirected M D) :
    (descentComparison N D (interiorSieve M D)).Full where
  map_surjective {ρ σ} u := by
    have hE₀D : E₀ ≤ D := MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem hE₀
    have hSE₀ : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hE₀D) := ⟨E₀, hE₀, le_rfl⟩
    refine ⟨⟨(u.app hE₀D hSE₀).val, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
    · intro a
      exact (u.app hE₀D hSE₀).intertwine ⟨a.val, halg a.2⟩
    · apply DescentDatum.Hom.ext'
      intro E hE hS
      apply FinRep.Hom.ext
      obtain ⟨F, hFint, hEF⟩ := id hS
      have hFD : F ≤ D := MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem hFint
      have hSF : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hFD) := ⟨F, hFint, le_rfl⟩
      obtain ⟨H, hHint, hFH, hE₀H⟩ := hdir hFint hE₀
      have hHD : H ≤ D := MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem hHint
      have hSH : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hHD) := ⟨H, hHint, le_rfl⟩
      calc (u.app hE₀D hSE₀).val
          = (u.app hHD hSH).val := theta_app_val_eq u hE₀D hE₀H hHD hSH hSE₀
        _ = (u.app hFD hSF).val :=
            (theta_app_val_eq u hFD hFH hHD hSH hSF).symm
        _ = (u.app hE hS).val :=
            (theta_app_val_eq u hE hEF hFD hSF hS).symm

/-! ## Essential surjectivity at the canonical cover (attained regime)

The construction: the witness component, pulled back along attainment,
is the global candidate; each component of the iso is a two-step path
through an interior hull of the member's interior envelope with the
witness.  Path independence is the cocycle condition in *potential*
form: every gluing matrix between members beneath a common interior `K`
is `(glue into K)⁻¹ · (glue into K)`, so all naturality squares
telescope. -/

section EssSurj

variable {N : ObservableNet X n} {D E₀ : Diamond X} {M : MixingKit X}

/-- A left inverse of a matrix with a right inverse is that inverse. -/
private theorem left_inverse_eq {d₁ d₂ : ℕ} {A : Matrix (Fin d₁) (Fin d₂) ℂ}
    {Y B : Matrix (Fin d₂) (Fin d₁) ℂ} (hYA : Y * A = 1) (hAB : A * B = 1) :
    Y = B := by
  calc Y = Y * (A * B) := by rw [hAB, Matrix.mul_one]
    _ = (Y * A) * B := by rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]
    _ = B := by rw [hYA, Matrix.one_mul]

variable {S : Sieve D} (Xd : DescentDatum N D S)

/-- The potential form of the cocycle: a gluing matrix between members
beneath a common third member is determined by the two gluings into
it. -/
private theorem glue_potential ⦃A B K : Diamond X⦄
    (hAB : A ≤ B) (hBD : B ≤ D) (hBK : B ≤ K) (hKD : K ≤ D)
    (hSK : S.arrows (homOfLE hKD)) (hSB : S.arrows (homOfLE hBD))
    (hSA : S.arrows (homOfLE (hAB.trans hBD))) :
    (Xd.glue hAB hBD hSB hSA).hom.val =
      (Xd.glue hBK hKD hSK hSB).inv.val *
        (Xd.glue (hAB.trans hBK) hKD hSK hSA).hom.val := by
  have hc := Xd.cocycle hAB hBK hKD hSK hSB hSA
  have h0 : (Xd.glue hAB hBD hSB hSA).hom.val
      = (Xd.glue hAB (hBK.trans hKD) hSB hSA).hom.val := rfl
  rw [h0]
  calc (Xd.glue hAB (hBK.trans hKD) hSB hSA).hom.val
      = ((Xd.glue hBK hKD hSK hSB).inv.val *
          (Xd.glue hBK hKD hSK hSB).hom.val) *
          (Xd.glue hAB (hBK.trans hKD) hSB hSA).hom.val := by
        rw [Xd.glue_inv_hom, Matrix.one_mul]
    _ = (Xd.glue hBK hKD hSK hSB).inv.val *
          ((Xd.glue hBK hKD hSK hSB).hom.val *
            (Xd.glue hAB (hBK.trans hKD) hSB hSA).hom.val) := by
        rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]
    _ = (Xd.glue hBK hKD hSK hSB).inv.val *
          (Xd.glue (hAB.trans hBK) hKD hSK hSA).hom.val := by rw [hc]

/-- The potential form for inverse gluing matrices. -/
private theorem glue_inv_potential ⦃A B K : Diamond X⦄
    (hAB : A ≤ B) (hBD : B ≤ D) (hBK : B ≤ K) (hKD : K ≤ D)
    (hSK : S.arrows (homOfLE hKD)) (hSB : S.arrows (homOfLE hBD))
    (hSA : S.arrows (homOfLE (hAB.trans hBD))) :
    (Xd.glue hAB hBD hSB hSA).inv.val =
      (Xd.glue (hAB.trans hBK) hKD hSK hSA).inv.val *
        (Xd.glue hBK hKD hSK hSB).hom.val := by
  refine (left_inverse_eq ?_ (Xd.glue_hom_inv hAB hBD hSB hSA)).symm
  calc ((Xd.glue (hAB.trans hBK) hKD hSK hSA).inv.val *
      (Xd.glue hBK hKD hSK hSB).hom.val) *
      (Xd.glue hAB hBD hSB hSA).hom.val
      = (Xd.glue (hAB.trans hBK) hKD hSK hSA).inv.val *
          ((Xd.glue hBK hKD hSK hSB).hom.val *
            (Xd.glue hAB (hBK.trans hKD) hSB hSA).hom.val) := by
        rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]
    _ = (Xd.glue (hAB.trans hBK) hKD hSK hSA).inv.val *
          (Xd.glue (hAB.trans hBK) hKD hSK hSA).hom.val := by
        rw [Xd.cocycle hAB hBK hKD hSK hSB hSA]
    _ = 1 := Xd.glue_inv_hom _ _ _ _

end EssSurj

section EssSurjConstruction

variable {N : ObservableNet X n} {D E₀ : Diamond X} {M : MixingKit X}

private theorem warr (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀) :
    (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE (MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem hE₀)) :=
  ⟨E₀, hE₀, le_rfl⟩

/-- The global candidate: the witness component transported along
attainment. -/
@[reducible] private noncomputable def cand (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (halg : N.alg D ≤ N.alg E₀)
    (Xd : DescentDatum N D (interiorSieve M D)) : FinRep ↥(N.alg D) :=
  ⟨(Xd.obj (MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem hE₀) (warr hE₀)).dim,
    (Xd.obj (MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem hE₀) (warr hE₀)).π.comp
      (Subalgebra.inclusion halg)⟩

private theorem hull_exists (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (hdir : InteriorDirected M D) ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (hE : E ≤ D)
    (hS : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hE)) :
    ∃ H : Diamond X, M.interiorMem D H ∧ E ≤ H ∧ E₀ ≤ H := by
  have hS' : ∃ F : Diamond X, M.interiorMem D F ∧ E ≤ F := hS
  obtain ⟨F, hFint, hEF⟩ := hS'
  obtain ⟨H, hHint, hFH, hE₀H⟩ := hdir hFint hE₀
  exact ⟨H, hHint, hEF.trans hFH, hE₀H⟩

private noncomputable def hull (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (hdir : InteriorDirected M D) ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (hE : E ≤ D)
    (hS : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hE)) : Diamond X :=
  (hull_exists hE₀ hdir hE hS).choose

private theorem hull_int (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (hdir : InteriorDirected M D) ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (hE : E ≤ D)
    (hS : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hE)) :
    M.interiorMem D (hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) :=
  (hull_exists hE₀ hdir hE hS).choose_spec.1

private theorem hull_le_D (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (hdir : InteriorDirected M D) ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (hE : E ≤ D)
    (hS : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hE)) :
    hull hE₀ hdir hE hS ≤ D :=
  MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem (hull_int hE₀ hdir hE hS)

private theorem le_hull (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (hdir : InteriorDirected M D) ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (hE : E ≤ D)
    (hS : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hE)) :
    E ≤ hull hE₀ hdir hE hS :=
  (hull_exists hE₀ hdir hE hS).choose_spec.2.1

private theorem w_le_hull (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (hdir : InteriorDirected M D) ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (hE : E ≤ D)
    (hS : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hE)) :
    E₀ ≤ hull hE₀ hdir hE hS :=
  (hull_exists hE₀ hdir hE hS).choose_spec.2.2

private theorem hull_arr (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (hdir : InteriorDirected M D) ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (hE : E ≤ D)
    (hS : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hE)) :
    (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)) :=
  ⟨hull hE₀ hdir hE hS, hull_int hE₀ hdir hE hS, le_rfl⟩

/-- The forward component: from the restricted candidate to the datum,
through the hull — `(glue of E into the hull)⁻¹ · (glue of E₀ into the
hull)`. -/
private noncomputable def uApp (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (halg : N.alg D ≤ N.alg E₀) (hdir : InteriorDirected M D)
    (Xd : DescentDatum N D (interiorSieve M D)) ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (hE : E ≤ D)
    (hS : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hE)) :
    (FinRep.pull (Subalgebra.inclusion (N.isotone hE))).obj
      (cand hE₀ halg Xd) ⟶ Xd.obj hE hS :=
  ⟨(Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).inv.val *
    (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).hom.val, by
    intro a
    have h1 : (Xd.obj hE hS).π a *
        (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
          (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).inv.val
        = (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
            (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).inv.val *
          (Xd.obj (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS)).π
            ⟨a.val, N.isotone (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) a.2⟩ :=
      (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
        (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).inv.intertwine a
    have h2 : (Xd.obj (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS)).π
          ⟨a.val, N.isotone (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) a.2⟩ *
          (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
            (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).hom.val
        = (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
            (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).hom.val *
          (Xd.obj (MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem hE₀) (warr hE₀)).π
            ⟨a.val, halg (N.isotone hE a.2)⟩ :=
      (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
        (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).hom.intertwine
        ⟨a.val, halg (N.isotone hE a.2)⟩
    calc (Xd.obj hE hS).π a *
        ((Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
            (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).inv.val *
          (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
            (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).hom.val)
        = ((Xd.obj hE hS).π a *
            (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
              (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).inv.val) *
            (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
              (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).hom.val := by
          rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]
      _ = ((Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
              (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).inv.val *
            (Xd.obj (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS)).π
              ⟨a.val, N.isotone (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) a.2⟩) *
            (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
              (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).hom.val := by
          rw [h1]
      _ = (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
            (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).inv.val *
            ((Xd.obj (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS)).π
              ⟨a.val, N.isotone (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) a.2⟩ *
              (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
                (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).hom.val) := by
          rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]
      _ = (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
            (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).inv.val *
            ((Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
                (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).hom.val *
              (Xd.obj (MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem hE₀) (warr hE₀)).π
                ⟨a.val, halg (N.isotone hE a.2)⟩) := by
          rw [h2]
      _ = ((Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
              (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).inv.val *
            (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
              (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).hom.val) *
            ((FinRep.pull (Subalgebra.inclusion (N.isotone hE))).obj
              (cand hE₀ halg Xd)).π a := by
          rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]; rfl⟩

/-- The backward component. -/
private noncomputable def vApp (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (halg : N.alg D ≤ N.alg E₀) (hdir : InteriorDirected M D)
    (Xd : DescentDatum N D (interiorSieve M D)) ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (hE : E ≤ D)
    (hS : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hE)) :
    Xd.obj hE hS ⟶
      (FinRep.pull (Subalgebra.inclusion (N.isotone hE))).obj
        (cand hE₀ halg Xd) :=
  ⟨(Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).inv.val *
    (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).hom.val, by
    intro a
    have h1 : (Xd.obj (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS)).π
          ⟨a.val, N.isotone (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) a.2⟩ *
          (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
            (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).hom.val
        = (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
            (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).hom.val * (Xd.obj hE hS).π a :=
      (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
        (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).hom.intertwine a
    have h2 : (Xd.obj (MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem hE₀) (warr hE₀)).π
          ⟨a.val, halg (N.isotone hE a.2)⟩ *
          (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
            (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).inv.val
        = (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
            (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).inv.val *
          (Xd.obj (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS)).π
            ⟨a.val, N.isotone (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) a.2⟩ :=
      (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
        (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).inv.intertwine
        ⟨a.val, halg (N.isotone hE a.2)⟩
    calc ((FinRep.pull (Subalgebra.inclusion (N.isotone hE))).obj
            (cand hE₀ halg Xd)).π a *
        ((Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
            (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).inv.val *
          (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
            (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).hom.val)
        = ((Xd.obj (MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem hE₀) (warr hE₀)).π
              ⟨a.val, halg (N.isotone hE a.2)⟩ *
            (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
              (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).inv.val) *
            (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
              (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).hom.val := by
          rw [← Matrix.mul_assoc]; rfl
      _ = ((Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
              (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).inv.val *
            (Xd.obj (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS)).π
              ⟨a.val, N.isotone (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) a.2⟩) *
            (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
              (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).hom.val := by
          rw [h2]
      _ = (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
            (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).inv.val *
            ((Xd.obj (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS)).π
              ⟨a.val, N.isotone (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) a.2⟩ *
              (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
                (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).hom.val) := by
          rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]
      _ = (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
            (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).inv.val *
            ((Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
                (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).hom.val *
              (Xd.obj hE hS).π a) := by
          rw [h1]
      _ = ((Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
              (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).inv.val *
            (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
              (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).hom.val) *
            (Xd.obj hE hS).π a := by
          rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]⟩

/-- `v ∘ u = 1` on the candidate side. -/
private theorem vu_id (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (halg : N.alg D ≤ N.alg E₀) (hdir : InteriorDirected M D)
    (Xd : DescentDatum N D (interiorSieve M D)) ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (hE : E ≤ D)
    (hS : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hE)) :
    (vApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd hE hS).val * (uApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd hE hS).val
      = 1 := by
  show ((Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).inv.val *
    (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).hom.val) *
    ((Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).inv.val *
    (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).hom.val) = 1
  rw [Matrix.mul_assoc, ← Matrix.mul_assoc
      (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
        (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).hom.val,
    Xd.glue_hom_inv, Matrix.one_mul, Xd.glue_inv_hom]

/-- `u ∘ v = 1` on the datum side. -/
private theorem uv_id (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (halg : N.alg D ≤ N.alg E₀) (hdir : InteriorDirected M D)
    (Xd : DescentDatum N D (interiorSieve M D)) ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (hE : E ≤ D)
    (hS : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hE)) :
    (uApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd hE hS).val * (vApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd hE hS).val
      = 1 := by
  show ((Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).inv.val *
    (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).hom.val) *
    ((Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).inv.val *
    (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).hom.val) = 1
  rw [Matrix.mul_assoc, ← Matrix.mul_assoc
      (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
        (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).hom.val,
    Xd.glue_hom_inv, Matrix.one_mul, Xd.glue_inv_hom]

/-- The canonical form of the forward component beneath any interior
diamond above the member's hull: the path telescopes to a `K`-potential. -/
private theorem uApp_canonical (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (halg : N.alg D ≤ N.alg E₀) (hdir : InteriorDirected M D)
    (Xd : DescentDatum N D (interiorSieve M D)) ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (hE : E ≤ D)
    (hS : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hE))
    ⦃K : Diamond X⦄ (hKint : M.interiorMem D K)
    (hHK : hull hE₀ hdir hE hS ≤ K) :
    (uApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd hE hS).val =
      (Xd.glue ((le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS).trans hHK)
          (MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem hKint) ⟨K, hKint, le_rfl⟩ hS).inv.val *
        (Xd.glue ((w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS).trans hHK)
          (MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem hKint) ⟨K, hKint, le_rfl⟩
          (warr hE₀)).hom.val := by
  have hKD : K ≤ D := MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem hKint
  have hSK : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hKD) := ⟨K, hKint, le_rfl⟩
  show (Xd.glue (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS).inv.val *
    (Xd.glue (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS) (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) (warr hE₀)).hom.val = _
  rw [glue_inv_potential Xd (le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS) hHK hKD hSK (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS) hS,
    glue_potential Xd (w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (hull_le_D hE₀ hdir hE hS) hHK hKD hSK (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS)
      (warr hE₀)]
  rw [Matrix.mul_assoc, ← Matrix.mul_assoc
      (Xd.glue hHK hKD hSK (hull_arr hE₀ hdir hE hS)).hom.val,
    Xd.glue_hom_inv, Matrix.one_mul]

/-- Naturality of the forward components: both sides are `K`-potentials
over a common interior roof, and the cocycle telescopes them to the same
matrix. -/
private theorem uApp_compat (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (halg : N.alg D ≤ N.alg E₀) (hdir : InteriorDirected M D)
    (Xd : DescentDatum N D (interiorSieve M D))
    ⦃E F : Diamond X⦄ (hEF : E ≤ F) (hFD : F ≤ D)
    (hSF : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hFD))
    (hSE : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE (hEF.trans hFD))) :
    (Xd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).hom.val *
        (uApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).val
      = (uApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd hFD hSF).val := by
  obtain ⟨K, hKint, hHEK, hHFK⟩ :=
    hdir (hull_int hE₀ hdir (hEF.trans hFD) hSE) (hull_int hE₀ hdir hFD hSF)
  have hKD : K ≤ D := MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem hKint
  have hSK : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hKD) := ⟨K, hKint, le_rfl⟩
  have hFK : F ≤ K := (le_hull hE₀ hdir hFD hSF).trans hHFK
  rw [uApp_canonical hE₀ halg hdir Xd (hEF.trans hFD) hSE hKint hHEK,
    uApp_canonical hE₀ halg hdir Xd hFD hSF hKint hHFK,
    glue_potential Xd hEF hFD hFK hKD hSK hSF hSE]
  have hcancel : (Xd.glue (hEF.trans hFK) hKD hSK hSE).hom.val *
      (Xd.glue ((le_hull hE₀ hdir (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).trans hHEK) hKD hSK
        hSE).inv.val = 1 :=
    Xd.glue_hom_inv (hEF.trans hFK) hKD hSK hSE
  calc ((Xd.glue hFK hKD hSK hSF).inv.val *
      (Xd.glue (hEF.trans hFK) hKD hSK hSE).hom.val) *
      ((Xd.glue ((le_hull hE₀ hdir (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).trans hHEK) hKD hSK
          hSE).inv.val *
        (Xd.glue ((w_le_hull hE₀ hdir (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).trans hHEK) hKD
          hSK (warr hE₀)).hom.val)
      = (Xd.glue hFK hKD hSK hSF).inv.val *
          (((Xd.glue (hEF.trans hFK) hKD hSK hSE).hom.val *
            (Xd.glue ((le_hull hE₀ hdir (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).trans hHEK) hKD
              hSK hSE).inv.val) *
            (Xd.glue ((w_le_hull hE₀ hdir (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).trans hHEK)
              hKD hSK (warr hE₀)).hom.val) := by
        rw [Matrix.mul_assoc, Matrix.mul_assoc]
    _ = (Xd.glue hFK hKD hSK hSF).inv.val *
          (Xd.glue ((w_le_hull hE₀ hdir (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).trans hHEK) hKD
            hSK (warr hE₀)).hom.val := by
        rw [hcancel, Matrix.one_mul]
    _ = (Xd.glue ((le_hull hE₀ hdir hFD hSF).trans hHFK) hKD hSK
          hSF).inv.val *
          (Xd.glue ((w_le_hull hE₀ hdir hFD hSF).trans hHFK) hKD hSK
            (warr hE₀)).hom.val := rfl

/-- Naturality of the backward components: `v_F · g` is a left inverse
of `u_E`, whose two-sided inverse is `v_E`. -/
private theorem vApp_compat (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (halg : N.alg D ≤ N.alg E₀) (hdir : InteriorDirected M D)
    (Xd : DescentDatum N D (interiorSieve M D))
    ⦃E F : Diamond X⦄ (hEF : E ≤ F) (hFD : F ≤ D)
    (hSF : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE hFD))
    (hSE : (interiorSieve M D).arrows (homOfLE (hEF.trans hFD))) :
    (vApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).val
      = (vApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd hFD hSF).val *
        (Xd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).hom.val := by
  refine (left_inverse_eq ?_
    (uv_id hE₀ halg hdir Xd (hEF.trans hFD) hSE)).symm
  calc ((vApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd hFD hSF).val *
      (Xd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).hom.val) *
      (uApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).val
      = (vApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd hFD hSF).val *
          ((Xd.glue hEF hFD hSF hSE).hom.val *
            (uApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd (hEF.trans hFD) hSE).val) := by
        rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]
    _ = (vApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd hFD hSF).val *
          (uApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd hFD hSF).val := by
        rw [uApp_compat hE₀ halg hdir Xd hEF hFD hSF hSE]
    _ = 1 := vu_id hE₀ halg hdir Xd hFD hSF

end EssSurjConstruction
/-- **Essential surjectivity at the canonical cover**: every descent
datum over the interior sieve of an attained, interior-directed diamond
is isomorphic to the restriction datum of a global representation —
the witness component transported along attainment.  This is where the
categorical layer consumes directedness: the components' dimensions
(multiplicities), invisible to states, must be transported coherently
to every fibre, including the scalar ones. -/
theorem descentComparison_essSurj_interior (M : MixingKit X)
    (N : ObservableNet X n) {D E₀ : Diamond X} (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (halg : N.alg D ≤ N.alg E₀) (hdir : InteriorDirected M D) :
    (descentComparison N D (interiorSieve M D)).EssSurj where
  mem_essImage Xd :=
    ⟨cand hE₀ halg Xd,
     ⟨{ hom :=
          { app := fun _ hE hS => uApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd hE hS
            compat := fun {E F} hEF hFD hSF hSE => by
              simp only [Iso.refl_hom, FinRep.id_val, Matrix.mul_one]
              exact uApp_compat hE₀ halg hdir Xd hEF hFD hSF hSE }
        inv :=
          { app := fun _ hE hS => vApp hE₀ halg hdir Xd hE hS
            compat := fun {E F} hEF hFD hSF hSE => by
              simp only [Iso.refl_hom, FinRep.id_val, Matrix.one_mul]
              exact vApp_compat hE₀ halg hdir Xd hEF hFD hSF hSE }
        hom_inv_id := DescentDatum.Hom.ext' (fun _ hE hS =>
          FinRep.Hom.ext (vu_id hE₀ halg hdir Xd hE hS))
        inv_hom_id := DescentDatum.Hom.ext' (fun _ hE hS =>
          FinRep.Hom.ext (uv_id hE₀ halg hdir Xd hE hS)) }⟩⟩

/-- **The attained-regime equivalence at the canonical cover**: with an
interior attainment witness and a directed interior family, the descent
comparison at the interior sieve is an equivalence of categories — the
categorified stack condition of the derived site, in the regime where a
single interior subdiamond already carries the global algebra. -/
theorem descentComparison_isEquivalence_interior (M : MixingKit X)
    (N : ObservableNet X n) {D E₀ : Diamond X} (hE₀ : M.interiorMem D E₀)
    (halg : N.alg D ≤ N.alg E₀) (hdir : InteriorDirected M D) :
    (descentComparison N D (interiorSieve M D)).IsEquivalence where
  faithful := descentComparison_faithful N D _
    (MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem hE₀) ⟨E₀, hE₀, le_rfl⟩
  full := descentComparison_full_interior M N hE₀ halg hdir
  essSurj := descentComparison_essSurj_interior M N hE₀ halg hdir

/-- **The two-qubit instance**: on the derived diamond site of 1+1
Minkowski space, the representation prestack of the two-qubit net
satisfies the categorified descent condition at the canonical interior
cover of the ambient diamond — attained at the interior witness, with
directedness supplied by the Minkowski chronology kit's
filtered/directed fields. -/
theorem qubitNet_stack_attained :
    (descentComparison qubitNet Dstar
      (interiorSieve ((minkowskiKit (E := ℝ)).toMixingKit) Dstar)).IsEquivalence :=
  descentComparison_isEquivalence_interior _ qubitNet E₃_interior
    (by rw [qubitNet_Dstar, qubitNet_E₃])
    ((minkowskiKit (E := ℝ)).interior_directed Dstar)

/-! ## Two-sided intertwiner extension along multiplicative generation -/

/-- **The two-sided multiplicative criterion**: a matrix intertwining
two global representations on every algebra of a sieve that generates
the global algebra multiplicatively intertwines them globally.  The
sibling of `intertwinerDescends_of_le_adjoin` at hom (rather than
endomorphism) grade. -/
theorem intertwines_of_le_adjoin {N : ObservableNet X n} {D : Diamond X}
    {S : Sieve D} {ρ σ : FinRep ↥(N.alg D)}
    (T : Matrix (Fin σ.dim) (Fin ρ.dim) ℂ)
    (hgen : N.alg D ≤ Algebra.adjoin ℂ
      (⋃ (E : Diamond X) (h : E ≤ D) (_ : S.arrows (homOfLE h)),
        (N.alg E : Set (Matrix n n ℂ))))
    (hloc : ∀ ⦃E : Diamond X⦄ (h : E ≤ D), S.arrows (homOfLE h) →
      ∀ b (hb : b ∈ N.alg E),
        σ.π ⟨b, N.isotone h hb⟩ * T = T * ρ.π ⟨b, N.isotone h hb⟩)
    (a : ↥(N.alg D)) : σ.π a * T = T * ρ.π a := by
  have hsub : Algebra.adjoin ℂ
      (⋃ (E : Diamond X) (h : E ≤ D) (_ : S.arrows (homOfLE h)),
        (N.alg E : Set (Matrix n n ℂ))) ≤ N.alg D := by
    rw [Algebra.adjoin_le_iff]
    intro b hb
    simp only [Set.mem_iUnion, SetLike.mem_coe] at hb
    obtain ⟨E, hE, _, hbE⟩ := hb
    exact N.isotone hE hbE
  -- induct over the adjoin membership, tracking membership in `N.alg D`
  have key : ∀ b (hb : b ∈ Algebra.adjoin ℂ
      (⋃ (E : Diamond X) (h : E ≤ D) (_ : S.arrows (homOfLE h)),
        (N.alg E : Set (Matrix n n ℂ)))) (hbD : b ∈ N.alg D),
      σ.π ⟨b, hbD⟩ * T = T * ρ.π ⟨b, hbD⟩ := by
    intro b hb
    induction hb using Algebra.adjoin_induction with
    | mem c hc =>
      intro hcD
      simp only [Set.mem_iUnion, SetLike.mem_coe] at hc
      obtain ⟨E, hE, hSE, hcE⟩ := hc
      exact hloc hE hSE c hcE
    | algebraMap r =>
      intro hrD
      have h1 : (⟨algebraMap ℂ (Matrix n n ℂ) r, hrD⟩ : ↥(N.alg D))
          = algebraMap ℂ ↥(N.alg D) r := rfl
      rw [h1, AlgHom.commutes, AlgHom.commutes,
        Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one, Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one,
        Matrix.smul_mul, Matrix.mul_smul, Matrix.one_mul, Matrix.mul_one]
    | add u v hu hv ihu ihv =>
      intro huvD
      have huD : u ∈ N.alg D := hsub hu
      have hvD : v ∈ N.alg D := hsub hv
      have h1 : (⟨u + v, huvD⟩ : ↥(N.alg D)) = ⟨u, huD⟩ + ⟨v, hvD⟩ := rfl
      rw [h1, map_add, map_add, Matrix.add_mul, Matrix.mul_add,
        ihu huD, ihv hvD]
    | mul u v hu hv ihu ihv =>
      intro huvD
      have huD : u ∈ N.alg D := hsub hu
      have hvD : v ∈ N.alg D := hsub hv
      have h1 : (⟨u * v, huvD⟩ : ↥(N.alg D)) = ⟨u, huD⟩ * ⟨v, hvD⟩ := rfl
      rw [h1, map_mul, map_mul]
      calc σ.π ⟨u, huD⟩ * σ.π ⟨v, hvD⟩ * T
          = σ.π ⟨u, huD⟩ * (σ.π ⟨v, hvD⟩ * T) := by rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]
        _ = σ.π ⟨u, huD⟩ * (T * ρ.π ⟨v, hvD⟩) := by rw [ihv hvD]
        _ = (σ.π ⟨u, huD⟩ * T) * ρ.π ⟨v, hvD⟩ := by rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]
        _ = (T * ρ.π ⟨u, huD⟩) * ρ.π ⟨v, hvD⟩ := by rw [ihu huD]
        _ = T * (ρ.π ⟨u, huD⟩ * ρ.π ⟨v, hvD⟩) := by rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]
  have := key a.val (hgen a.2) a.2
  simpa using this

/-! ## The two-qubit geometry: the null corner, and a gapped variant -/

/-- The degenerate diamond at the null corner where the two halves of
the landed pair cover touch. -/
def originD : Diamond (Mink ℝ) := ⟨⟨0, 0⟩, ⟨0, 0⟩, le_rfl⟩

theorem originD_le_D₁ : originD ≤ D₁ := by
  constructor
  · show ‖(0 : ℝ) - (-1)‖ ≤ (0 : ℝ) - (-1)
    rw [Real.norm_eq_abs]; norm_num
  · show ‖(-1 : ℝ) - 0‖ ≤ (1 : ℝ) - 0
    rw [Real.norm_eq_abs]; norm_num

theorem originD_le_D₂ : originD ≤ D₂ := by
  constructor
  · show ‖(0 : ℝ) - 1‖ ≤ (0 : ℝ) - (-1)
    rw [Real.norm_eq_abs]; norm_num
  · show ‖(1 : ℝ) - 0‖ ≤ (1 : ℝ) - 0
    rw [Real.norm_eq_abs]; norm_num

/-- **Fullness at the landed pair cover**: the null-corner contact
between the two halves ties the wing components of any descent morphism
together, and multiplicative generation of the global algebra by the
wings (`adjoin_union_eq_top`) extends the common matrix to a global
intertwiner.  The morphism clause of the stack condition holds *whole*
at the very cover where the object clause fails
(`wingDatum_not_in_essImage`) — the categorified sharpening of the
landed two-column contrast. -/
theorem descentComparison_pair_full :
    (descentComparison qubitNet Dstar (pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar)).Full where
  map_surjective {ρ σ} u := by
    have hS1 : (pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar).arrows (homOfLE D₁_le_Dstar) :=
      Or.inl le_rfl
    have hS2 : (pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar).arrows (homOfLE D₂_le_Dstar) :=
      Or.inr le_rfl
    have hoD : originD ≤ Dstar := originD_le_D₁.trans D₁_le_Dstar
    have hSo : (pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar).arrows (homOfLE hoD) :=
      Or.inl originD_le_D₁
    -- the corner ties the two wing matrices together
    have t1 : (u.app hoD hSo).val = (u.app D₁_le_Dstar hS1).val :=
      theta_app_val_eq u hoD originD_le_D₁ D₁_le_Dstar hS1 hSo
    have t2 : (u.app hoD hSo).val = (u.app D₂_le_Dstar hS2).val :=
      theta_app_val_eq u hoD originD_le_D₂ D₂_le_Dstar hS2 hSo
    refine ⟨⟨(u.app D₁_le_Dstar hS1).val, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
    · -- global intertwining from the two wings via adjoin
      intro a
      refine intertwines_of_le_adjoin (N := qubitNet)
        (S := pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar) _ ?_ ?_ a
      · rw [qubitNet_Dstar]
        calc (⊤ : Subalgebra ℂ TwoQubits)
            = Algebra.adjoin ℂ
                ((leftFactor : Set TwoQubits) ∪ rightFactor) :=
              adjoin_union_eq_top.symm
          _ ≤ Algebra.adjoin ℂ
              (⋃ (E : Diamond (Mink ℝ)) (h : E ≤ Dstar)
                (_ : (pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar).arrows (homOfLE h)),
                  (qubitNet.alg E : Set TwoQubits)) := by
              refine Algebra.adjoin_mono ?_
              rintro b (hb | hb)
              · refine Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨D₁, Set.mem_iUnion.mpr
                  ⟨D₁_le_Dstar, Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨Or.inl le_rfl, ?_⟩⟩⟩
                rw [qubitNet_D₁]
                exact hb
              · refine Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨D₂, Set.mem_iUnion.mpr
                  ⟨D₂_le_Dstar, Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨Or.inr le_rfl, ?_⟩⟩⟩
                rw [qubitNet_D₂]
                exact hb
      · -- local intertwining on each sieve member, via the wing values
        intro E hE hSE b hb
        rcases (show E ≤ D₁ ∨ E ≤ D₂ from hSE) with hE1 | hE2
        · have hSb : (pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar).arrows (homOfLE hE) :=
            Or.inl hE1
          have hval : (u.app hE hSb).val = (u.app D₁_le_Dstar hS1).val :=
            theta_app_val_eq u hE hE1 D₁_le_Dstar hS1 hSb
          have h := (u.app hE hSb).intertwine ⟨b, hb⟩
          rw [hval] at h
          exact h
        · have hSb : (pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar).arrows (homOfLE hE) :=
            Or.inr hE2
          have hval : (u.app hE hSb).val = (u.app D₁_le_Dstar hS1).val := by
            rw [theta_app_val_eq u hE hE2 D₂_le_Dstar hS2 hSb, ← t2, t1]
          have h := (u.app hE hSb).intertwine ⟨b, hb⟩
          rw [hval] at h
          exact h
    · -- the image morphism reproduces every component
      apply DescentDatum.Hom.ext'
      intro E hE hS
      apply FinRep.Hom.ext
      rcases (show E ≤ D₁ ∨ E ≤ D₂ from hS) with hE1 | hE2
      · exact (theta_app_val_eq u hE hE1 D₁_le_Dstar hS1 hS).symm
      · show (u.app D₁_le_Dstar hS1).val = (u.app hE hS).val
        exact (t1.symm.trans t2).trans
          (theta_app_val_eq u hE hE2 D₂_le_Dstar hS2 hS).symm

/-! ## The wing irreducibles, and the multiplicity obstruction -/

/-- Extraction of the left tensor factor: the entry-block formula
`a ↦ (a (i,0) (j,0))ᵢⱼ`, an algebra homomorphism on the left wing. -/
noncomputable def leftExtract : ↥leftFactor →ₐ[ℂ] Qubit where
  toFun a := Matrix.of fun i j => a.val (i, 0) (j, 0)
  map_one' := by
    ext i j
    show ((1 : TwoQubits)) (i, 0) (j, 0) = (1 : Qubit) i j
    simp [Matrix.one_apply, Prod.ext_iff]
  map_mul' a b := by
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := mem_leftFactor.mp a.2
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := mem_leftFactor.mp b.2
    have hax : (Matrix.of fun i j => a.val (i, 0) (j, 0)) = x := by
      ext i j
      show a.val (i, 0) (j, 0) = x i j
      rw [← hx]
      simp [Matrix.kroneckerMap_apply]
    have hby : (Matrix.of fun i j => b.val (i, 0) (j, 0)) = y := by
      ext i j
      show b.val (i, 0) (j, 0) = y i j
      rw [← hy]
      simp [Matrix.kroneckerMap_apply]
    have hab : (a * b).val = (x * y) ⊗ₖ (1 : Qubit) := by
      show a.val * b.val = _
      rw [← hx, ← hy, ← Matrix.mul_kronecker_mul, one_mul]
    ext i j
    show (a * b).val (i, 0) (j, 0) = _
    rw [hab, hax, hby]
    simp [Matrix.kroneckerMap_apply]
  map_zero' := by
    ext i j
    show ((0 : TwoQubits)) (i, 0) (j, 0) = (0 : Qubit) i j
    simp
  map_add' a b := by
    ext i j
    show (a + b).val (i, 0) (j, 0) = _
    simp [Matrix.add_apply]
  commutes' c := by
    ext i j
    show (algebraMap ℂ TwoQubits c) (i, 0) (j, 0) = (algebraMap ℂ Qubit c) i j
    simp [Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one, Matrix.smul_apply, Matrix.one_apply,
      Prod.ext_iff]

/-- Extraction of the right tensor factor. -/
noncomputable def rightExtract : ↥rightFactor →ₐ[ℂ] Qubit where
  toFun a := Matrix.of fun i j => a.val (0, i) (0, j)
  map_one' := by
    ext i j
    show ((1 : TwoQubits)) (0, i) (0, j) = (1 : Qubit) i j
    simp [Matrix.one_apply, Prod.ext_iff]
  map_mul' a b := by
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := mem_rightFactor.mp a.2
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := mem_rightFactor.mp b.2
    have hax : (Matrix.of fun i j => a.val (0, i) (0, j)) = x := by
      ext i j
      show a.val (0, i) (0, j) = x i j
      rw [← hx]
      simp [Matrix.kroneckerMap_apply]
    have hby : (Matrix.of fun i j => b.val (0, i) (0, j)) = y := by
      ext i j
      show b.val (0, i) (0, j) = y i j
      rw [← hy]
      simp [Matrix.kroneckerMap_apply]
    have hab : (a * b).val = (1 : Qubit) ⊗ₖ (x * y) := by
      show a.val * b.val = _
      rw [← hx, ← hy, ← Matrix.mul_kronecker_mul, one_mul]
    ext i j
    show (a * b).val (0, i) (0, j) = _
    rw [hab, hax, hby]
    simp [Matrix.kroneckerMap_apply]
  map_zero' := by
    ext i j
    show ((0 : TwoQubits)) (0, i) (0, j) = (0 : Qubit) i j
    simp
  map_add' a b := by
    ext i j
    show (a + b).val (0, i) (0, j) = _
    simp [Matrix.add_apply]
  commutes' c := by
    ext i j
    show (algebraMap ℂ TwoQubits c) (0, i) (0, j) = (algebraMap ℂ Qubit c) i j
    simp [Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one, Matrix.smul_apply, Matrix.one_apply,
      Prod.ext_iff]

open scoped Classical in
/-- A subdiamond of both halves of the pair cover carries scalar
observables only: neither site fits in the overlap. -/
theorem overlap_scalar {E : Diamond (Mink ℝ)} (h1 : E ≤ D₁) (h2 : E ≤ D₂) :
    qubitNet.alg E = ⊥ := by
  have hp : ¬ inDiamond p E := fun hp => p_not_mem_D₂ (inDiamond_mono h2 hp)
  have hq : ¬ inDiamond q E := fun hq => q_not_mem_D₁ (inDiamond_mono h1 hq)
  show (if _ then _ else _) = ⊥
  rw [if_neg hp, if_neg hq]

open scoped Classical in
/-- The wing action of a pair-sieve member: the left irreducible on
members of the left half, the right irreducible otherwise. -/
noncomputable def wingPi ⦃E : Diamond (Mink ℝ)⦄ (h : E ≤ Dstar)
    (hS : (pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar).arrows (homOfLE h)) :
    ↥(qubitNet.alg E) →ₐ[ℂ] Qubit :=
  if h₁ : E ≤ D₁ then
    leftExtract.comp (Subalgebra.inclusion
      ((qubitNet.isotone h₁).trans qubitNet_D₁.le))
  else
    rightExtract.comp (Subalgebra.inclusion
      ((qubitNet.isotone
        ((show E ≤ D₁ ∨ E ≤ D₂ from hS).resolve_left h₁)).trans
        qubitNet_D₂.le))

/-- The wing actions cohere along refinements: within a wing by
construction, and across the two wings on the scalar overlap. -/
theorem wingPi_compat ⦃E F : Diamond (Mink ℝ)⦄ (hEF : E ≤ F)
    (hFD : F ≤ Dstar)
    (hSF : (pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar).arrows (homOfLE hFD))
    (hSE : (pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar).arrows (homOfLE (hEF.trans hFD)))
    (a : ↥(qubitNet.alg E)) :
    wingPi (hEF.trans hFD) hSE a
      = wingPi hFD hSF (Subalgebra.inclusion (qubitNet.isotone hEF) a) := by
  unfold wingPi
  by_cases hE1 : E ≤ D₁
  · rw [dif_pos hE1]
    by_cases hF1 : F ≤ D₁
    · rw [dif_pos hF1]
      rfl
    · rw [dif_neg hF1]
      have hF2 : F ≤ D₂ :=
        (show F ≤ D₁ ∨ F ≤ D₂ from hSF).resolve_left hF1
      have hbot : qubitNet.alg E = ⊥ := overlap_scalar hE1 (hEF.trans hF2)
      have ha : a.val ∈ (⊥ : Subalgebra ℂ TwoQubits) := hbot ▸ a.2
      rw [Algebra.mem_bot] at ha
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := ha
      have ha' : a = algebraMap ℂ ↥(qubitNet.alg E) c :=
        Subtype.ext hc.symm
      rw [ha']
      simp only [AlgHom.commutes]
  · rw [dif_neg hE1]
    by_cases hF1 : F ≤ D₁
    · exact absurd (hEF.trans hF1) hE1
    · rw [dif_neg hF1]
      rfl

open scoped Classical in
/-- **The wing-multiplicity-one datum** over the spacelike pair cover:
each wing carries its two-dimensional irreducible representation via
the extraction homomorphisms; the scalar overlap is tied by the
identity.  Every gluing matrix is `1`; the cocycle is `1 · 1 = 1`. -/
noncomputable def wingDatum :
    DescentDatum qubitNet Dstar (pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar) where
  obj _ h hS := ⟨2, wingPi h hS⟩
  glue {E F} hEF hFD hSF hSE :=
    { hom := ⟨1, fun a => by
        rw [Matrix.mul_one, Matrix.one_mul]
        exact (wingPi_compat hEF hFD hSF hSE a).symm⟩
      inv := ⟨1, fun a => by
        rw [Matrix.mul_one, Matrix.one_mul]
        exact wingPi_compat hEF hFD hSF hSE a⟩
      hom_inv_id := FinRep.Hom.ext (Matrix.one_mul 1)
      inv_hom_id := FinRep.Hom.ext (Matrix.one_mul 1) }
  cocycle _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ := Matrix.one_mul 1

/-- **The global algebra has no unital two-dimensional representation**:
the four diagonal matrix units map to idempotents with pairwise equal
traces summing to `tr 1₂ = 2`, so each has trace `½` — and a `2 × 2`
idempotent of trace `½` is refuted by entry arithmetic.  This is the
arithmetic core of the multiplicity obstruction, with no simplicity or
spectral machinery. -/
theorem no_unital_hom_top_to_dim_two
    (π : ↥(qubitNet.alg Dstar) →ₐ[ℂ] Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) : False := by
  have hmem : ∀ u : TwoQubits, u ∈ qubitNet.alg Dstar := by
    intro u; rw [qubitNet_Dstar]; exact Algebra.mem_top
  let unit : (Fin 2 × Fin 2) → (Fin 2 × Fin 2) → ↥(qubitNet.alg Dstar) :=
    fun k k' => ⟨Matrix.single k k' 1, hmem _⟩
  have hmul : ∀ k k' : Fin 2 × Fin 2, unit k k' * unit k' k = unit k k := by
    intro k k'
    apply Subtype.ext
    show Matrix.single k k' (1 : ℂ) * Matrix.single k' k 1
        = Matrix.single k k 1
    rw [Matrix.single_mul_single_same, one_mul]
  have htr : ∀ k k' : Fin 2 × Fin 2,
      (π (unit k k)).trace = (π (unit k' k')).trace := by
    intro k k'
    calc (π (unit k k)).trace
        = (π (unit k k' * unit k' k)).trace := by rw [hmul]
      _ = (π (unit k k') * π (unit k' k)).trace := by rw [map_mul]
      _ = (π (unit k' k) * π (unit k k')).trace := Matrix.trace_mul_comm _ _
      _ = (π (unit k' k * unit k k')).trace := by rw [map_mul]
      _ = (π (unit k' k')).trace := by rw [hmul]
  have hsumu : (∑ k : Fin 2 × Fin 2, unit k k) = 1 := by
    have hcoe : (qubitNet.alg Dstar).val (∑ k : Fin 2 × Fin 2, unit k k)
        = ∑ k : Fin 2 × Fin 2, Matrix.single k k (1 : ℂ) :=
      map_sum _ _ _
    apply Subtype.ext
    calc (∑ k : Fin 2 × Fin 2, unit k k).val
        = ∑ k : Fin 2 × Fin 2, Matrix.single k k (1 : ℂ) := hcoe
      _ = 1 := Matrix.sum_single_one
  have h4 : (4 : ℂ) * (π (unit ((0 : Fin 2), (0 : Fin 2))
      ((0 : Fin 2), (0 : Fin 2)))).trace = 2 := by
    have hs : (∑ k : Fin 2 × Fin 2, π (unit k k)).trace
        = ((1 : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ)).trace := by
      rw [← map_sum, hsumu, map_one]
    rw [Matrix.trace_sum] at hs
    rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl
      (fun k _ => htr k ((0 : Fin 2), (0 : Fin 2)))] at hs
    rw [Finset.sum_const, Finset.card_univ] at hs
    simp only [Fintype.card_prod, Fintype.card_fin, nsmul_eq_mul,
      Matrix.trace_one, Fintype.card_fin] at hs
    exact_mod_cast hs
  set A := π (unit ((0 : Fin 2), (0 : Fin 2)) ((0 : Fin 2), (0 : Fin 2)))
    with hA
  have hid : A * A = A := by
    rw [hA, ← map_mul, hmul]
  have htrA : A 0 0 + A 1 1 = 1 / 2 := by
    have h := h4
    rw [Matrix.trace_fin_two] at h
    linear_combination h / 4
  have h00 := congrFun (congrFun hid 0) 0
  have h01 := congrFun (congrFun hid 0) 1
  have h10 := congrFun (congrFun hid 1) 0
  have h11 := congrFun (congrFun hid 1) 1
  simp only [Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_two] at h00 h01 h10 h11
  have hkey : (A 0 0 - A 1 1) * (A 0 0 + A 1 1 - 1) = 0 := by
    linear_combination h00 - h11
  rcases mul_eq_zero.mp hkey with had | had
  · have ha : A 0 0 = 1 / 4 := by linear_combination had / 2 + htrA / 2
    have hb : A 0 1 = 0 := by
      linear_combination 2 * A 0 1 * htrA - 2 * h01
    rw [ha, hb] at h00
    norm_num at h00
  · have : (-(1 / 2) : ℂ) = 0 := by linear_combination had - htrA
    norm_num at this

/-- **The multiplicity obstruction, kernel-visible**: no global
representation restricts to the wing-multiplicity-one datum.  Any
isomorphism of descent data includes an isomorphism of the `D₁`
components, forcing the global dimension to two by the trace argument —
and the global algebra has no unital two-dimensional representation.
Essential surjectivity of the comparison fails at the pair cover on
*multiplicity*: local dimensions compose tensorially, cover-gluing
composes them as a common value. -/
theorem wingDatum_not_in_essImage :
    ¬ ∃ ρ : FinRep ↥(qubitNet.alg Dstar),
      Nonempty ((descentComparison qubitNet Dstar
        (pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar)).obj ρ ≅ wingDatum) := by
  rintro ⟨⟨d, π⟩, ⟨e⟩⟩
  set ρ : FinRep ↥(qubitNet.alg Dstar) := ⟨d, π⟩ with hρ
  have hS1 : (pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar).arrows (homOfLE D₁_le_Dstar) :=
    Or.inl le_rfl
  have hcomp1 : e.hom.app D₁_le_Dstar hS1 ≫ e.inv.app D₁_le_Dstar hS1
      = 𝟙 _ := by
    have := congrArg
      (fun (w : (descentComparison qubitNet Dstar
        (pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar)).obj ρ ⟶ (descentComparison qubitNet Dstar
          (pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar)).obj ρ) => w.app D₁_le_Dstar hS1)
      e.hom_inv_id
    simpa only [DescentDatum.comp_app, DescentDatum.id_app] using this
  have hcomp2 : e.inv.app D₁_le_Dstar hS1 ≫ e.hom.app D₁_le_Dstar hS1
      = 𝟙 _ := by
    have := congrArg
      (fun (w : wingDatum ⟶ wingDatum) => w.app D₁_le_Dstar hS1)
      e.inv_hom_id
    simpa only [DescentDatum.comp_app, DescentDatum.id_app] using this
  have hiso : (FinRep.pull (Subalgebra.inclusion
      (qubitNet.isotone D₁_le_Dstar))).obj ρ ≅ wingDatum.obj D₁_le_Dstar hS1 :=
    ⟨e.hom.app D₁_le_Dstar hS1, e.inv.app D₁_le_Dstar hS1, hcomp1, hcomp2⟩
  have hdim : d = 2 := FinRep.dim_eq_of_iso hiso
  subst hdim
  exact no_unital_hom_top_to_dim_two π

/-- Essential surjectivity fails at the spacelike pair cover. -/
theorem descentComparison_pair_not_essSurj :
    ¬ (descentComparison qubitNet Dstar (pairSieve D₁ D₂ Dstar)).EssSurj := by
  intro h
  exact wingDatum_not_in_essImage (h.mem_essImage wingDatum)

/-! ## The gapped pair: generation without connectivity -/

/-- A gapped right half: a smaller diamond around the right site,
disjoint from `D₁`.  Same wing algebra, same multiplicative generation —
no corner contact. -/
noncomputable def gappedD₂ : Diamond (Mink ℝ) :=
  ⟨⟨-(1/2), 1⟩, ⟨1/2, 1⟩, by norm_num [Mink.le_def, Real.norm_eq_abs]⟩

theorem q_mem_gappedD₂ : inDiamond q gappedD₂ := by
  constructor
  · show ‖(1 : ℝ) - 1‖ ≤ (0 : ℝ) - (-(1/2))
    rw [Real.norm_eq_abs]; norm_num
  · show ‖(1 : ℝ) - 1‖ ≤ (1/2 : ℝ) - 0
    rw [Real.norm_eq_abs]; norm_num

theorem p_not_mem_gappedD₂ : ¬ inDiamond p gappedD₂ := by
  rintro ⟨h, -⟩
  have : ‖(-1 : ℝ) - 1‖ ≤ (0 : ℝ) - (-(1/2)) := h
  rw [Real.norm_eq_abs] at this
  norm_num at this

theorem gappedD₂_le_Dstar : gappedD₂ ≤ Dstar := by
  constructor
  · show ‖(1 : ℝ) - 0‖ ≤ (-(1/2) : ℝ) - (-3)
    rw [Real.norm_eq_abs]; norm_num
  · show ‖(0 : ℝ) - 1‖ ≤ (3 : ℝ) - (1/2)
    rw [Real.norm_eq_abs]; norm_num

open scoped Classical in
theorem qubitNet_alg_gappedD₂ : qubitNet.alg gappedD₂ = rightFactor := by
  show (if _ then _ else (if _ then rightFactor else _)) = rightFactor
  rw [if_neg p_not_mem_gappedD₂, if_pos q_mem_gappedD₂]

/-- The gapped halves are disjoint: no subdiamond fits in both. -/
theorem gapped_no_overlap {E : Diamond (Mink ℝ)} (h1 : E ≤ D₁)
    (h2 : E ≤ gappedD₂) : False := by
  have ha : ‖E.lo.x - (-1 : ℝ)‖ ≤ E.lo.t - (-1) := h1.1
  have hb : ‖(-1 : ℝ) - E.lo.x‖ ≤ (1 : ℝ) - E.lo.t := E.le.trans h1.2
  have hc : ‖E.lo.x - (1 : ℝ)‖ ≤ E.lo.t - (-(1/2)) := h2.1
  have hd : ‖(1 : ℝ) - E.lo.x‖ ≤ (1/2 : ℝ) - E.lo.t := E.le.trans h2.2
  rw [Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_le] at ha hb hc hd
  obtain ⟨ha1, ha2⟩ := ha
  obtain ⟨hb1, hb2⟩ := hb
  obtain ⟨hc1, hc2⟩ := hc
  obtain ⟨hd1, hd2⟩ := hd
  linarith

/-- The witness matrix of the gapped fullness failure: a left-wing
projection, viewed in the reindexed global algebra. -/
noncomputable def wGap : Matrix (Fin 4) (Fin 4) ℂ :=
  Matrix.reindexAlgEquiv ℂ ℂ (finProdFinEquiv : Fin 2 × Fin 2 ≃ Fin 4)
    ((Matrix.single (0 : Fin 2) 0 1) ⊗ₖ (1 : Qubit))

theorem wGap_commutes_right (y : Qubit) :
    Matrix.reindexAlgEquiv ℂ ℂ (finProdFinEquiv : Fin 2 × Fin 2 ≃ Fin 4)
        ((1 : Qubit) ⊗ₖ y) * wGap
      = wGap * Matrix.reindexAlgEquiv ℂ ℂ
          (finProdFinEquiv : Fin 2 × Fin 2 ≃ Fin 4) ((1 : Qubit) ⊗ₖ y) := by
  unfold wGap
  rw [← map_mul, ← map_mul, ← Matrix.mul_kronecker_mul,
    ← Matrix.mul_kronecker_mul, one_mul, mul_one, one_mul, mul_one]

theorem wGap_ne_one : wGap ≠ 1 := by
  intro h
  have h1 : (Matrix.single (0 : Fin 2) 0 (1 : ℂ)) ⊗ₖ (1 : Qubit)
      = (1 : TwoQubits) := by
    apply (Matrix.reindexAlgEquiv ℂ ℂ
      (finProdFinEquiv : Fin 2 × Fin 2 ≃ Fin 4)).injective
    rw [map_one]
    exact h
  have h2 := congrFun (congrFun h1 ((1 : Fin 2), (0 : Fin 2)))
    ((1 : Fin 2), (0 : Fin 2))
  simp [Matrix.kroneckerMap_apply, Matrix.single, Matrix.of_apply] at h2

open scoped Classical in
/-- The gapped witness endomorphism component: the identity on the left
wing, the projection `wGap` on the gapped right wing. -/
private noncomputable def gapApp ⦃E : Diamond (Mink ℝ)⦄ (hE : E ≤ Dstar)
    (hS : (pairSieve D₁ gappedD₂ Dstar).arrows (homOfLE hE)) :
    (FinRep.pull (Subalgebra.inclusion (qubitNet.isotone hE))).obj
        (tautRep (qubitNet.alg Dstar)) ⟶
      (FinRep.pull (Subalgebra.inclusion (qubitNet.isotone hE))).obj
        (tautRep (qubitNet.alg Dstar)) :=
  if h1 : E ≤ D₁ then 𝟙 _ else
    ⟨wGap, fun a => by
      have h2 : E ≤ gappedD₂ :=
        (show E ≤ D₁ ∨ E ≤ gappedD₂ from hS).resolve_left h1
      have haR : a.val ∈ rightFactor :=
        qubitNet_alg_gappedD₂ ▸ qubitNet.isotone h2 a.2
      obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := mem_rightFactor.mp haR
      have hπ : ((FinRep.pull (Subalgebra.inclusion (qubitNet.isotone hE))).obj
          (tautRep (qubitNet.alg Dstar))).π a
          = Matrix.reindexAlgEquiv ℂ ℂ
              (finProdFinEquiv : Fin 2 × Fin 2 ≃ Fin 4) a.val := rfl
      rw [hπ, ← hy]
      exact wGap_commutes_right y⟩

private theorem gapApp_val_left ⦃E : Diamond (Mink ℝ)⦄ (hE : E ≤ Dstar)
    (hS : (pairSieve D₁ gappedD₂ Dstar).arrows (homOfLE hE))
    (h1 : E ≤ D₁) : (gapApp hE hS).val = 1 := by
  unfold gapApp
  rw [dif_pos h1]
  rfl

private theorem gapApp_val_right ⦃E : Diamond (Mink ℝ)⦄ (hE : E ≤ Dstar)
    (hS : (pairSieve D₁ gappedD₂ Dstar).arrows (homOfLE hE))
    (h1 : ¬ E ≤ D₁) : (gapApp hE hS).val = wGap := by
  unfold gapApp
  rw [dif_neg h1]

/-- **Fullness fails at the gapped pair cover**: with the corner contact
removed, the two wings carry independent endomorphism freedoms — the
descent endomorphism that is the identity on the left wing and a
left-factor projection on the right wing is lawful, but every image
morphism has one matrix across all components.  Same wings, same
multiplicative generation as the landed cover: connectivity, not
generation, is what fullness consumes. -/
theorem descentComparison_gapped_not_full :
    ¬ (descentComparison qubitNet Dstar
      (pairSieve D₁ gappedD₂ Dstar)).Full := by
  intro hFull
  obtain ⟨T, hT⟩ := hFull.map_surjective
    (X := tautRep (qubitNet.alg Dstar)) (Y := tautRep (qubitNet.alg Dstar))
    { app := fun _ hE hS => gapApp hE hS
      compat := fun {E F} hEF hFD hSF hSE => by
        simp only [Iso.refl_hom, FinRep.id_val, Matrix.one_mul,
          Matrix.mul_one]
        by_cases hE1 : E ≤ D₁
        · by_cases hF1 : F ≤ D₁
          · rw [gapApp_val_left _ _ hE1, gapApp_val_left _ _ hF1]
          · exact (gapped_no_overlap hE1 (hEF.trans
              ((show F ≤ D₁ ∨ F ≤ gappedD₂ from hSF).resolve_left hF1))).elim
        · by_cases hF1 : F ≤ D₁
          · exact (hE1 (hEF.trans hF1)).elim
          · rw [gapApp_val_right _ _ hE1, gapApp_val_right _ _ hF1] }
  have hS1 : (pairSieve D₁ gappedD₂ Dstar).arrows (homOfLE D₁_le_Dstar) :=
    Or.inl le_rfl
  have hSg : (pairSieve D₁ gappedD₂ Dstar).arrows
      (homOfLE gappedD₂_le_Dstar) := Or.inr le_rfl
  have hg_not : ¬ gappedD₂ ≤ D₁ := fun hcon => gapped_no_overlap hcon le_rfl
  have h1 : T.val = 1 := by
    have h := congrArg (fun w => (w.app D₁_le_Dstar hS1).val) hT
    rw [gapApp_val_left _ _ le_rfl] at h
    exact h
  have h2 : T.val = wGap := by
    have h := congrArg (fun w => (w.app gappedD₂_le_Dstar hSg).val) hT
    rw [gapApp_val_right _ _ hg_not] at h
    exact h
  exact wGap_ne_one (h2.symm.trans h1)


/-! ## The degenerate fence: the empty sieve covers a corner -/

/-- The degenerate corner diamond of the ambient diamond. -/
def cornerD : Diamond (Mink ℝ) := ⟨Dstar.lo, Dstar.lo, le_rfl⟩

/-- The empty sieve. -/
def emptySieve (D' : Diamond (Mink ℝ)) : Sieve D' where
  arrows _ _ := False
  downward_closed h _ := h

/-- No subdiamond of a degenerate diamond is chronologically interior:
interiority would give `lo ≪ lo`. -/
theorem cornerD_no_interior (E : Diamond (Mink ℝ)) :
    ¬ ((minkowskiKit (E := ℝ)).toMixingKit).interiorMem cornerD E := by
  rintro ⟨h1, h2⟩
  have hc : (minkowskiKit (E := ℝ)).chron cornerD.lo cornerD.lo :=
    minkowskiKit.chron_of_chron_le
      (minkowskiKit.chron_of_chron_le h1 E.le)
      (minkowskiKit.le_of_chron h2)
  have : ‖(Dstar.lo.x : ℝ) - Dstar.lo.x‖ < Dstar.lo.t - Dstar.lo.t := hc
  simp at this

/-- The derived topology certifies the empty sieve at the corner:
the covering condition is vacuous. -/
theorem emptySieve_covering_corner :
    emptySieve cornerD ∈
      ((minkowskiKit (E := ℝ)).toMixingKit).diamondTopology cornerD :=
  fun E _ hint => absurd hint (cornerD_no_interior E)

/-- **The comparison is not faithful over the empty sieve**: all descent
morphisms are equal there, but the tautological representation has
distinct endomorphisms.  Representation categories, unlike state sets,
are not points over scalar fibres — so the categorified condition
cannot survive the degenerate covers the derived topology certifies,
and the equivalence theorem is honestly a statement about the canonical
interior covers. -/
theorem descentComparison_corner_not_faithful :
    ¬ (descentComparison qubitNet cornerD (emptySieve cornerD)).Faithful := by
  intro hF
  have hzero : ∀ a : ↥(qubitNet.alg cornerD),
      (tautRep (qubitNet.alg cornerD)).π a * (0 : Matrix (Fin 4) (Fin 4) ℂ)
        = 0 * (tautRep (qubitNet.alg cornerD)).π a := by
    intro a; rw [Matrix.mul_zero, Matrix.zero_mul]
  let z : tautRep (qubitNet.alg cornerD) ⟶ tautRep (qubitNet.alg cornerD) :=
    ⟨0, hzero⟩
  have heq : (descentComparison qubitNet cornerD (emptySieve cornerD)).map z
      = (descentComparison qubitNet cornerD (emptySieve cornerD)).map
        (𝟙 (tautRep (qubitNet.alg cornerD))) := by
    apply DescentDatum.Hom.ext'
    intro E hE hS
    exact ((hS : False)).elim
  have hval := congrArg FinRep.Hom.val (hF.map_injective heq)
  have hz : FinRep.Hom.val z = 0 := rfl
  rw [hz, FinRep.id_val] at hval
  have h00 := congrFun (congrFun hval 0) 0
  simp [Matrix.zero_apply] at h00

/-! ## The bad object fails fullness at the canonical cover -/

/-- **The bad object fails fullness even at the canonical interior
cover**: with all interior algebras scalar, any constant matrix is a
lawful descent endomorphism of the restricted tautological
representation — but an image morphism's matrix must intertwine the
global algebra, and an off-diagonal unit does not.  Content at the
global scale is invisible to the interior at morphism grade:
attainment is load-bearing in the equivalence, exactly as it was at
separation grade. -/
theorem badNet_not_full_interior :
    ¬ (descentComparison badNet Dstar
      (interiorSieve ((minkowskiKit (E := ℝ)).toMixingKit) Dstar)).Full := by
  intro hFull
  have hcomm : ∀ ⦃E : Diamond (Mink ℝ)⦄ (hE : E ≤ Dstar)
      (hS : (interiorSieve ((minkowskiKit (E := ℝ)).toMixingKit)
        Dstar).arrows (homOfLE hE)) (a : ↥(badNet.alg E)),
      (tautRep (badNet.alg Dstar)).π
          (Subalgebra.inclusion (badNet.isotone hE) a) *
          Matrix.single (0 : Fin 4) 1 1
        = Matrix.single (0 : Fin 4) 1 1 *
          (tautRep (badNet.alg Dstar)).π
            (Subalgebra.inclusion (badNet.isotone hE) a) := by
    intro E hE hS a
    obtain ⟨F, hFint, hEF⟩ := hS
    have hbot : a.val ∈ (⊥ : Subalgebra ℂ TwoQubits) :=
      ((badNet.isotone hEF).trans
        (le_of_eq (badNet_interior_bot hFint))) a.2
    rw [Algebra.mem_bot] at hbot
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hbot
    have ha : Subalgebra.inclusion (badNet.isotone hE) a
        = algebraMap ℂ ↥(badNet.alg Dstar) c := Subtype.ext hc.symm
    rw [ha, AlgHom.commutes, Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one,
      Matrix.smul_mul, Matrix.mul_smul, Matrix.one_mul, Matrix.mul_one]
  obtain ⟨T, hT⟩ := hFull.map_surjective
    (X := tautRep (badNet.alg Dstar)) (Y := tautRep (badNet.alg Dstar))
    { app := fun _ hE hS => ⟨Matrix.single (0 : Fin 4) 1 1, hcomm hE hS⟩
      compat := fun {E F} hEF hFD hSF hSE => by
        simp only [Iso.refl_hom, FinRep.id_val, Matrix.one_mul,
          Matrix.mul_one] }
  have hSE₃ : (interiorSieve ((minkowskiKit (E := ℝ)).toMixingKit)
      Dstar).arrows (homOfLE E₃_le_Dstar) := ⟨E₃, E₃_interior, le_rfl⟩
  have hTval : T.val = Matrix.single (0 : Fin 4) 1 1 := by
    have := congrArg (fun w => (w.app E₃_le_Dstar hSE₃).val) hT
    simpa using this
  set elt : ↥(badNet.alg Dstar) :=
    ⟨(Matrix.reindexAlgEquiv ℂ ℂ
        (finProdFinEquiv : Fin 2 × Fin 2 ≃ Fin 4)).symm
      (Matrix.single (1 : Fin 4) 0 1),
     by rw [badNet_Dstar]; exact Algebra.mem_top⟩ with helt
  have hint := T.intertwine elt
  rw [hTval] at hint
  have hπ : (tautRep (badNet.alg Dstar)).π elt
      = Matrix.single (1 : Fin 4) 0 1 := by
    rw [tautRep_π_apply, helt]
    exact AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply _ _
  rw [hπ, Matrix.single_mul_single_same, Matrix.single_mul_single_same]
    at hint
  have h11 := congrFun (congrFun hint 1) 1
  simp [Matrix.single, Matrix.of_apply] at h11

end QuantumStack
